OL,3,GNEWSAClip of long-lost early children's
OL,4,ATV show found
OL,5,
OL,6,FA chance find on an audio cassette has
OL,7,Fled to the recovery of the only known
OL,8,Fsurviving material from one of
OL,9,FBritain's first popular children's
OL,10,Ftelevision shows.
OL,12,FWhirligig ran for more than 90 episodes
OL,13,Ffrom 1950 to 1956, but no recordings
OL,14,Ffrom the series were thought to exist.
OL,16,FThe find was made by Stuart Woodhead
OL,17,Ffrom Grimsby, who runs the Joy Laurey
OL,18,FArchive, which is dedicated to one of
OL,19,FWhirligig's resident puppeteers.
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
